From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:01:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/22] ASoC: SDCA: default reset_max_delay in
 populate_function path

sdca_parse_function() defaults reset_max_delay to 100ms when the
DisCo mipi-sdca-function-reset-max-delay property is absent (see
sdca_functions.c parse_function_extension_id()).  The
populate_function callback path added for DT/non-DisCo platforms
does no such thing, so a codec driver that forgets to set
function->reset_max_delay leaves it at zero.

sdca_reset_function() then calls regmap_read_poll_timeout() with
timeout_us == 0.  That helper's internal check requires a non-zero
timeout to break, so the poll spins forever on any hardware that
does not clear the status bit on the first read.

Guard against this in class_function_probe(): after the callback
returns success, if reset_max_delay is still zero apply the same
100ms default the DisCo path uses.  Codec drivers that need a
different value continue to set it explicitly in their static
function data.

Signed-off-by: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8e50032471fad15237e71cc3b75f8beb98aaa5c8)
---
 sound/soc/sdca/sdca_class_function.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_class_function.c b/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_class_function.c
index 13b70f0f0dbf..ef9d7667e662 100644
--- a/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_class_function.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_class_function.c
@@ -374,6 +374,16 @@ static int class_function_probe(struct auxiliary_device *auxdev,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * sdca_parse_function() defaults reset_max_delay to 100ms when
+	 * the DisCo property is absent.  Mirror that here for the
+	 * populate_function path so codec drivers that forget to set it
+	 * do not end up passing 0 to regmap_read_poll_timeout() inside
+	 * sdca_reset_function(), which would spin forever.
+	 */
+	if (!drv->function->reset_max_delay)
+		drv->function->reset_max_delay = 100000;
+
 	ndefaults = sdca_regmap_count_constants(dev, drv->function);
 	if (ndefaults < 0)
 		return ndefaults;
